#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "381f7ffe-ae4b-5e45-9fa9-e2a6bd8348b3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3456a3ad-31e0-57f6-90c3-d82785326e0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267986} {:answer/id #uuid "9de5434f-c0cd-5d91-821a-3f6b7e651785" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9de5434f-c0cd-5d91-821a-3f6b7e651785" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267987} :answer-field/id #uuid "759a12ae-3e96-59e3-abda-e5560f7ca639" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267985} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77a0875d-4e53-50f9-bba5-b24ff1162ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77a0875d-4e53-50f9-bba5-b24ff1162ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267989} :answer-field/id #uuid "44b19442-3b87-580a-b04c-67f1ece21b73" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267988}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e5fd29d-a330-5cdf-80f4-ab919ec2657f" :question/math-academy-id "q-275670" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T({v}_{1}+2{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, then find $T({v}_{2}).$\n\n| $T({v}_{2})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v+kw)=T(v)+T(kw)=T(v)+kT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}+2{v}_{2}) & =T({v}_{1})+2T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+2T({v}_{2}) \\\\ 2T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 2T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fbd335c-28cc-5f02-b773-f685e8b15417" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Sum Under a Map Using Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a7b55e9-6029-56ad-a4f6-47b27eaa0e6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a7b55e9-6029-56ad-a4f6-47b27eaa0e6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267992} :answer-field/id #uuid "893a54a2-5bc9-56bd-ab33-2bda7b9c89d9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267991} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c6d9375-e558-5f24-9660-83e927c45c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c6d9375-e558-5f24-9660-83e927c45c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267994} :answer-field/id #uuid "05804e9f-14f4-5ba7-b730-51c4e9faba88" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267993} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b81879b5-89c2-5b51-adfa-90b9006cad8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b81879b5-89c2-5b51-adfa-90b9006cad8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267996} :answer-field/id #uuid "5236ff12-25f2-5395-89b5-2e4549869ffa" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267995}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ed9d455b-c98a-5122-ac8f-6166788eb347" :question/math-academy-id "q-317824" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$, find  $T(7{v}_{1}+12{v}_{2}).$\n\n| $\\,T(7{v}_{1}+12{v}_{2})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, since ${v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{v}_{1}+12{v}_{2} & =12{v}_{1}-5{v}_{1}+12{v}_{2} \\\\  & =12({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})-5{v}_{1} \\\\  & =12(0)-5{v}_{1} \\\\  & =-5{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(7{v}_{1}+12{v}_{2})=T(-5{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-5{v}_{1}) & =-5T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =-5[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -20 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(7{v}_{1}+12{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -20 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267997 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "381f7ffe-ae4b-5e45-9fa9-e2a6bd8348b3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b49d99a5-3b5d-5492-a3c5-c53ada18e278" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267999} {:answer/id #uuid "f35c7ae2-f6ee-559f-b79a-001c0a203661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268000} {:answer/id #uuid "99fe3f55-1473-5392-ae6b-62285007f9b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268001} {:answer/id #uuid "c1221eb8-ba5d-5058-ad1a-5c42cec2bd7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268002} {:answer/id #uuid "898fae0f-e9e0-5cc2-b048-9f1b8ed746fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1221eb8-ba5d-5058-ad1a-5c42cec2bd7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268002} :answer-field/id #uuid "1683c11f-ae04-533e-92da-b8760c5e5933" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267998}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40b5e068-2dad-584f-b3a2-08b1c2d3ff01" :question/math-academy-id "q-74773" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(2{v}_{1}+3{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, then find $\\,T({v}_{1}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+hw)=T(kv)+T(hw)=kT(v)+hT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(2{v}_{1}+3{v}_{2}) & =2T({v}_{1})+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =2T({v}_{1})+3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a2275b7-0cd4-5acd-ad72-a48b0b2500ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268006} {:answer/id #uuid "c277f7b3-76e0-5e40-b67a-d1147b5db584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268007} {:answer/id #uuid "62482cca-61a3-5b23-9619-47da3c54bfcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268008} {:answer/id #uuid "28156a0d-ee37-549d-810f-e1b8cedcc9ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268009} {:answer/id #uuid "1f961e99-5b0e-588c-b4b1-413172278b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a2275b7-0cd4-5acd-ad72-a48b0b2500ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268006} :answer-field/id #uuid "48d49dd3-04d8-5449-9d2a-f2ea6067e69d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268005}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20a14b0f-437e-5229-9343-d166ad27d365" :question/math-academy-id "q-8022" :question/problem "Let \n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+y \\\\ 2y\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n- $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\n- $T$ is a linear transformation" :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}]=kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}], \\\\  & T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}kx+ky \\\\ 2(ky)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}k(x+y) \\\\ k(2y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =k[\\begin{aligned}x+y \\\\ 2y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 2({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{y}_{1} \\\\ 2{y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088361 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "865035a9-dfe6-51bf-a5dc-624240267541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087097} {:answer/id #uuid "981d3229-34da-5547-9622-76e7a57b9b97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087098} {:answer/id #uuid "ff08f834-c93c-58b6-a6eb-be4ab302b1ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087099} {:answer/id #uuid "5826ab39-99cb-5f0d-a91a-c8e47d4e7431" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087100} {:answer/id #uuid "58fc334c-401e-58ca-8084-7bbee1c81411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "865035a9-dfe6-51bf-a5dc-624240267541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087097} :answer-field/id #uuid "212166f2-0485-5ec6-aaa6-538998150651" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087096}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9a96319-3bb3-5dd4-a3ac-27f5effab07d" :question/math-academy-id "q-8331" :question/problem "Let\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}y \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix}$.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $T(kv) = kT(v)$ for any real $2 \\cdot 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n2. $T(v_{1} + v_{2}) = T(v_{1}) + T(v_{2})$ for any real $2 \\cdot 1$ column vectors $v_{1}$ and $v_{2}$\n3. $T$ is a linear transformation" :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}]=kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}], \\\\  & T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}ky \\\\ kx\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =k[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."}]}
